WEBVTT
Language: en-GB

00:00:01.082 --> 00:00:04.482 line:84%
What is biogas? And biomethane?

00:00:04.957 --> 00:00:11.377 line:84%
It all starts with what nobody wants:
food scraps, manure, crop leftovers…

00:00:11.852 --> 00:00:14.252 line:84%
Inside the biodigester —

00:00:14.292 --> 00:00:18.652 line:84%
a sealed tank with no oxygen
– microbes throw a party…

00:00:19.127 --> 00:00:22.067 line:84%
and release a gas: biogas!

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:27.982 line:84%
It's mostly methane and carbon dioxide,
with a pinch of other gases…

00:00:28.457 --> 00:00:30.957 line:84%
some of them really smelly!

00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:36.052 line:84%
But by burning biogas,
we can make heat and electricity.

00:00:36.527 --> 00:00:40.507 line:84%
And there's more: take out the
carbon dioxide and impurities,

00:00:40.547 --> 00:00:44.707 line:84%
and biomethane is born
– almost pure methane!

00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:49.762 line:84%
It's just like natural gas, only
renewable: it can travel through

00:00:49.802 --> 00:00:53.942 line:84%
the gas grid to homes and industries,
or fuel lorries and buses.

00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:57.117 line:84%
And what's left in the biodigester becomes

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:00.657 line:84%
biofertiliser for the fields…
closing the loop!

00:01:01.132 --> 00:01:06.912 line:84%
Biogas and biomethane: today's
waste is tomorrow's energy!

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:13.060 line:84%
CP2B: living energy,
science that transforms!
